>> servings: 4

Preheat the oven to 200°C.

Grate @zucchini{2} and finely chop the @brown onion{1}. Very thinly slice the remaining @zucchini{1} lengthwise into ribbons for the top.

In a large bowl, combine the grated zucchini, onion, @tasty cheese{0.5%cup}(shredded), @self-raising flour{1%cup}, 0.33 cup extra virgin olive oil, and @egg{5}. Mix until well combined. Season generously with salt and pepper.

Spread half the mixture into a baking dish lined with baking paper. Spoon over half of the @caramelised onion relish{0.67%cup} and gently swirl through. Top with the remaining mixture and smooth the surface.

Arrange the zucchini ribbons over the top, then dollop over the remaining caramelised onion relish and scatter with @feta{50%g}(crumbled).

Bake for ~{45%minutes}, or until golden and set in the centre. Allow to cool for at least ~{45%minutes} before slicing. Finish with @chives{2%tbsp}(finely chopped) and serve.
